I was just about to post the same kind of idea: include items of
neutral or negative effect.  Of course, the names wouuldn't be
obviously bad (like the Dan Quayle).  Sleeper works as a misleading
name.  In fact, if the name implies nothing (Mjollnir doesn't tell
me anything) you could include a little hint of the pluses, without
saying anything about the minuses.
In reference to the "Gee, I wish I could have armor that increased
my strength", the parse tree could help with that.  You might end up
with the +0 (or worse) leather armor of +1 strength, but it at least
answers the literal request.  With all the questions that the tree
would ask (blessed? enchanted?) you could counterbalance with random
chances that not only will the wish not be entirely granted, but
your character's uppitiness might be punished in some subtle way.
After all there is a difference between wishing for a +3 crysknife
or a non-perishable blessed +3 crysknife of sped, slow digestion, and
+5 all attributes.
